# Ship to Git and Vercel

When landing work is done (layout, styles, assets, copy, or rules), ship it in the same turn.

## Current target: motion preview only

Work on `experiment/card-motion`. Do not change https://next-level-landing.vercel.app unless the user explicitly asks.

1. Commit the relevant files to Git. Do not wait for “запушь” / “собери”.
2. Push the current branch to `origin`.
3. Deploy **preview** with `npx vercel --yes --scope next-level-1999` (never `--prod`).
4. Point the public alias at that deployment:
   `npx vercel alias set <preview-url> next-level-landing-motion.vercel.app --scope next-level-1999`
5. Return https://next-level-landing-motion.vercel.app/ plus the existing `_vercel_share` query (preview URLs are SSO-gated without it).

## Production (only if the user asks)

If the user explicitly asks to update https://next-level-landing.vercel.app:

1. Commit and push as above (usually on `main`).
2. Deploy with `npx vercel --prod --yes --scope next-level-1999`.
3. Return https://next-level-landing.vercel.app

## Do not

- Do not commit `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`, `.env`, or other generated/secret files.
- Do not amend a pushed commit. Create a new commit instead.
- Do not force-push `main`.
- Do not alias the experiment over `next-level-landing.vercel.app`.
